WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.652
The module uses a small healthcare-style teaching database.

00:00:03.652 --> 00:00:05.882
Patients is the main entity.

00:00:05.882 --> 00:00:10.467
Admissions, lab results, and prescriptions connect back to patients.

00:00:10.467 --> 00:00:13.382
Admissions also connect to departments.

00:00:13.382 --> 00:00:18.947
The review queue contains one patient ID and one deliberate NULL.

00:00:18.947 --> 00:00:23.917
That NULL is important because we will use it to demonstrate the NOT IN trap.

00:00:23.917 --> 00:00:26.917
The database loads automatically in the browser.

00:00:26.917 --> 00:00:32.592
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team finding customers who purchased a target product.

00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:38.237
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:45.662
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:45.662 --> 00:00:51.347
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:51.347 --> 00:00:57.244
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
